        <button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy-citation hidden>Copy BibTeX</button><span class="copy-status" data-copy-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
</article>
<section class="section-row" id="next-study" aria-labelledby="next-study-heading">
  <h2 class="section-label" id="next-study-heading">Proposed study</h2>
  <div class="section-body">
    <h3>Does graph structure help handover policies generalize?</h3>
    <p>I would compare a graph-attention policy with a graph-free multilayer perceptron (MLP) using the same observations, action constraints, training budget, and evaluation scenarios. I would test changes in cell layout and delayed signal or load measurements separately so each comparison answers a specific question.</p>
    <p>I would compare throughput, handover frequency, and short cell stays across multiple seeds, then report paired differences and uncertainty. The first deliverable would be a small runnable benchmark with synthetic layouts, settings, and per-scenario outputs that another researcher could inspect.</p>
    <p class="small-note">The repository includes a <a href="{{ profile.code }}/tree/main/hpcorbit">graph-free comparison workflow</a>. Results and the proposed public benchmark are pending.</p>
  </div>
</section>
